Z||000002||Formula||07-09-2001||11:05 PM||||My favorite is the old stel phantom at kennywood park in pittsburgh pa, its one of the 80+ mph ones.....as a matter of fact, the first time I rode it they said the track heated up too much or something and it hit 96 mph,  It jerks you around too much on the turns but its worth it!<P>The new one is the Phantom's revenge and I havent had a chance to ride it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||07-10-2001||12:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>My favorite is the old stel phantom at kennywood park in pittsburgh pa, its one of the 80+ mph ones.....as a matter of fact, the first time I rode it they said the track heated up too much or something and it hit 96 mph,  It jerks you around too much on the turns but its worth it!<P>The new one is the Phantom's revenge and I havent had a chance to ride it.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I still haven't been over to Kennywood this year since the Phantom's Revenge opened.  Apparently they took out the loops (but kept the 220+ foot drop) and put in cars that ride smoother.  They also eliminated the shoulder harnesses since there aren't any loops anymore.<P>I was sorry to see the original Phantom go, it was my favorite steel coaster.  Wish Kennywood would get around to installing a suspended coaster though...<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||07-10-2001||01:12 AM||||All i have to say is X-FLIGHT at 6 flags worlds of adventure (formely geauga lake) in Ohio... DAMN it rules... it HANGS you from the track..  You start in upright position with cars under you then the backs tilt down so your laying on your back as you accend hill... the only thing holding you back is a padded harness over shoulders (like a racing harness) and a small lap belt!  Then at top it flips you over and your HANGING!!! Feels like flying.. damn its sooooo sweet!  And I live close enough to have a season pass WOO HOO!  lol!  check it out there site is <A HREF="http://www.sixflags.com/parks/worldsofadventure/home.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sixflags.com/parks/worldsofadventure/home.asp</A>  and here is a link for the X-Flight <A HREF="http://www.sixflags.com/parks/worldsofadventure/Rides/xflight.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sixflags.com/parks/worldsofadventure/Rides/xflight.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierokid87||07-10-2001||02:48 AM||||Well so far the best one Ive ridden is Raptor.  I know old stuff but I have not been to Cedar point or Six Flags OH yet this year.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
