Z||000010||firstfiero||07-10-2001||09:01 AM||||    That would be cool. Cedar point is supposed to have the top coasters in the country! They have the same ride that fieromaster is talking about at the sixflags I was at in dc. They call it the bat wing their.<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||09:08 AM||||Gridlock! you were at Darien Lake last week?! so was I, last friday with my son.<P> Superman at Darien lake must be the same as the Superman at the other 6 flags parks - awesome ride.<P>  they also have one there called the MindEraser - its one of those hanging coasters. I went on it twice last year, the first time I felt dizzy for about an hour after. The second time I held my breath all the way down the first drop and almost blacked out - started getting tunnel vision and everything looked sparkely and fuzzy, and I couldnt remember where I was for a few seconds - what fun! I skipped the MindEraser this year - no fun driving 80 miles home when you feel dizzy and disorentated.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||09:12 AM||||BTW my son wants to goto Cedar Point this summer too - hes taking an advanced math class in summer school to get ahead, so I dont think we can go during the week until late august though.||||reg||1
Z||000013||deceler8||07-10-2001||09:23 AM||||Cedar Point Rules !<P>Used to go there every year on opening day...haven't been there since 1992 when I moved from Ohio.<P>If anyone gets a trip together, I'll definitely be there. I'd suggest September after Labor day (they're open weekends through the end of September)...fewer crowds.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shaft||07-10-2001||01:50 PM||||Cedar Point is the best. The best coasters I've ridden so far are the Millennium Force and the Raptor. The M Force in the front seat is the biggest rush you'll ever have. I'm going to Six Flags to ride X-Flight on July 28th so I'll let you know if it's better.||||reg||6
Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||07-10-2001||02:44 PM||||now that they are building coasters with linear magnetic brakes - I wanna know who is gonna build the first coaster with linear motors - one that starts out level - accelerates up to 90mph, and then throws you up straight UP a 300 foot hill, and down the other side!<P>  they could build one that goes all the way around the park - up one giant hill and down another, with linear motors in between to speed the cars back up.<P>  they could also make em that way with single cars - everyone would be in the 'front seat' then - spaced out a couple hundred yards each.||||reg||1
Z||000016||BC-GT||07-10-2001||05:20 PM||||I wanted to ride Goliath at Sixflags in California last month on my trip but some lady had died on it the night before and they had it shut down <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Seems she had a brain aneurysm <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Never even bothered going into the park because of that.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fformula88||07-10-2001||05:26 PM||||My vote goes for the Comet when it was at Crystal Beach!  Riding that thing backwards wasn't exciting, it was downright frightening!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I haven't been on it since they moved it, but I heard you cannot ride it backwards anymore, which kind of ruins it.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cliff Pennock||07-10-2001||05:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>now that they are building coasters with linear magnetic brakes - I wanna know who is gonna build the first coaster with linear motors - one that starts out level - accelerates up to 90mph, and then throws you up straight UP a 300 foot hill, and down the other side!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, those have been around for quite some time. Space Mountain in Disneyland is one, you start out at a 45 degree angle (facing up). Superman is another (you start level and accelerate to 70mph and then go <u>straight</u> up, and another one that I know of is here in Holland where you also start out straight and are shot into a looping.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||DecadenceR||07-10-2001||05:58 PM||||At Six Flags by me, they have that... Batman Chiller. i think you start off at 70mph from full stop. I don't rememebr exactly. First time I went on it, my hair was down to my chin. It was gelled back. When we got back to the station, it was all pointing out foward. I looked like a cartoon.||||reg||1
Z||000020||firstfiero||07-10-2001||09:31 PM||||    yep,we have on to. Jokers Jynx...0 to 70 mph in 3 seconds. It is a face peeling rush!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Sleeper||07-11-2001||12:09 AM||||Six Flags Mountain here in cali is the best. my fav is...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vipercoaster.jpg"> <BR>Viper: The largest looping roller coaster in the world towers 188 feet high! Turns upside down seven times at a speed of 70 mph. but all of them are cool, you just always gotta sit in the very front.<P>and this is almost complete too: Deja Vu<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/img_md_dejavu.jpg"> <BR>The Story<BR>Next generation suspended looping boomerang rollercoaster - Deja Vu will be the world's tallest and fastest of it's kind. Déjà Vu combines state-of-the-art thrill ride technology with a brand new twist - riders fly forwards and backwards over twisting, looping inverted steel track. Strapped into sleek ski-lift style chairs suspended from the track above, Déjà Vu sends riders dangling face-down out of the station and up the first striking blue tower * to then * simply * drop into a complete vertical 20-story free-fall reaching speeds of 65 miles-per-hour before racing head-over-heels on the outside of a 102 foot-tall vertical loop followed by an enormous 110-foot-tall butterfly turn * before rocketing up the second 200-foot-tall tower - only this time riders are on their back with nothing but the sky above. The heart-pounding rush accelerates as the entire thrill is experienced again, only this time backwards! It's Déjà Vu!   <P>click on <A HREF="http://www.sixflags.com/parks/magicmountain/home.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sixflags.com/parks/magicmountain/home.asp</A>  too see more of Magic Mountain.||||reg||1
Z||000022||fierofreek2001||07-11-2001||12:27 AM||||cedar point is good BUT, only if you like waiting in lines for oh, i dont know know.. THREE HOURS OR MORE...   i had a bad experience there, i waited for that one ride ... i cant think of the name, magnum or somethin? the tallest one there...  anyways, i waited for 2 hours, got up to the front.. and... "attention, the rollercoaster is broke down for the rest of the day.. ENJOY YOUR DAY AT CEDAR POINT!" .. i was like #(*$ THIS PLACE... man i was so pissed, cuz i only had one day there, im in virginia<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000023||The Fieromaster||07-11-2001||01:04 AM||||Cedar Point is the "bomb mack diggety" (lmfao) Its the best and Im only like 1 hour and a half from it.. god its just one of the reasons Ohio kicks A$$<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
