Z||000025||Cliff Pennock||07-31-2001||08:58 AM||||I went to Cedar Point yesterday, man that was cool! I didn't get to ride the Millenium Force  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> because there was a 75 minute line and it was waaaaay to hot to wait so long in line, but I did most of the other rides.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||deceler8||07-31-2001||09:21 AM||||Hell Cliff...you should've let some of us Ohio boys know you were going to go...I've been looking for a reason to go back to Cedar Point for years.<P>Hope you at least got to ride the Magnum and the Raptor.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Oreif||07-31-2001||09:37 AM||||I was at Kings Island last week. The Beast and Son of Beast were very excellent wooden rollercoasters! (Son of Beast is the world's only looping Wooden rollercoaster not to mention the highest and fastest Wooden roller coaster.) I have yet to go to Cedar Point but hoping to soon!||||reg||1
Z||000028||fierobaby||07-31-2001||11:20 AM||||CLIFFY!!!!!!!!! YOU WERE SO CLOSE!!!!!! you should have told us!!! :-( oh well best rollercoaster I have ridden was the riddler at Six Flags Magic Mountain :-) it was cool even though I hate roller coasters *ducks the flame*||||reg||1
Z||000029||Ken Wittlief||07-31-2001||01:15 PM||||the Millimum Force at Cedar Point is big and its fast<P> but for sheer roller coaster thrill value the Mean Streak wins hands down. Its all wood, 160 something foot first drop, goes over 60mph, and the ride is so wild going down the first hill you cant see straight, literally!<P> part of the fun of a roller coaster is the inherent fear that the whole thing might just fly off the tracks at any instant - you dont get that on coasters with tubular steel rails and nylon wheels.<P>  but some of the curves on the Mean Streak are so fast I cant imagine how it stays on the track.<P>  and the best part, while the line at the Millinum Force was 60 to 90 minutes long all day, there were a few times when we were able to get on the Mean Streak with no line at all.<P>  Cedar Point! - after that everything else is just a carnival!||||reg||11
Z||000030||sombre||07-31-2001||07:24 PM||||   Funny I was just thinking that Cedar Point would be a cool place for a fiero get get-together while I was there last friday... <P>  The onsite hotels are prices but they have special rates for group things..someone should check into it...<P>  Friday is the best weekend day...still a little crowded but only 1 hour for the millenium..<P>  M. force uses linear motors as do all the superman rides...<P>  M.Force is humbling when you are in line pictures just don't do it justice....The accent is steeper than most decents on other coasters...But it goes by too fast....I still like magnum,mantis, an mean streak for more thrill than just a big hill and speed.<P>                        Greg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Ken Wittlief||08-01-2001||11:13 AM||||you were there last friday? thats when I was in the park all day - Im willing to bet I saw you at some point.<P> those things that look like linear motors on the MF are the brakes, it uses a rope to pull the car up the first hill - for some reason a rope is faster than a chain<BR>  <BR> maybe it has linear motors somewhere in the middle of the ride to speed it back up - I didnt really notice.||||reg||1
Z||000032||88CoupeV6||08-01-2001||11:54 AM||||Anyone belong to ACE? I've been a member for 2 years now. Check out my website <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/fiero64" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/fiero64</A> <P>I think the best ride is Volcano the blast coaster. It is at Paramount King's Dominion. It's an inverted coaster, 0-70 in 4 sec. linear magnetic takeoff then outside for a sweeping turn then back inside for more lim's(linear induction motors) speed you up toward a brick wall as it lifts you strait up inches away to a height of 155 ft out the top of a volcano and twists around it as flames shoot out the top. It is the best in my mind. <P>I also like superman ride of steel at six flags New England. 228 foot drop   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My list could go on and on about why each coaster is great. I love them all. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by 88CoupeV6 (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000033||88CoupeV6||08-01-2001||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I went to Cedar Point yesterday, man that was cool! I didn't get to ride the Millenium Force   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> because there was a 75 minute line and it was waaaaay to hot to wait so long in line, but I did most of the other rides.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, I want to go there if the lines are that short. I usualy wait 2-3 hours to get on superman and I waited 4 hours for volcano when it opened.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have to save up to make it to ohio. I keep dreaming of Cedar Point<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000034||Tigger||08-01-2001||12:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I went to Cedar Point yesterday, man that was cool! I didn't get to ride the Millenium Force   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> because there was a 75 minute line and it was waaaaay to hot to wait so long in line, but I did most of the other rides.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I haven't rode the Millenium yet either.  Eventually I'll take the hour or so wait.  The way I see it, in the time you stand waiting for that one, you can ride 3, 4, or more other great rides in the same amount of time.<P>I liked the rock & roll rollercoaster at Disney MGM.  Not really the fastest or the most intense, but does have a high excitement factor.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000035||DecadenceR||08-01-2001||04:07 PM||||I just rode Nitro at my Six Flags the other day. It is such an awsome ride!!!!!!<BR>Anyway, I think I'l have to come to Ohio to try out your six flags too. Since my pass is good in all of them... Woo-hoo!!!||||reg||1
Z||000036||Ken Wittlief||08-02-2001||09:44 AM||||Six flags in Ohio?!<P>dont hop on the plane yet - Cedar Point is NOT a Six Flags park - its independant.<P>I dont know if there is a Six Flags park in Ohio - if there is, skip it and go to Cedar Point instead!||||reg||11
